558
00:21:29,120 --> 00:21:32,799
illustrates it nicely.

559
00:21:31,360 --> 00:21:34,559
You might remember from high school

560
00:21:32,799 --> 00:21:36,320
physics that whenever an electric

561
00:21:34,559 --> 00:21:38,559
current flows through a wire, it

562
00:21:36,320 --> 00:21:40,559
produces a magnetic field that circles

563
00:21:38,559 --> 00:21:42,559
around the wire.

564
00:21:40,559 --> 00:21:44,960
If we take that wire and bend it into a

565
00:21:42,559 --> 00:21:47,440
loop, the small circular magnetic fields

566
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:48,960
from each segment combine together, the

567
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:50,960
result is a field that looks like the

568
00:21:48,960 --> 00:21:52,799
one produced by a tiny bar magnet

569
00:21:50,960 --> 00:21:54,720
pointing in the direction given by the

570
00:21:52,799 --> 00:21:56,480
right- hand rule. Curl your fingers

571
00:21:54,720 --> 00:21:59,520
along the current and your thumb points

572
00:21:56,480 --> 00:22:01,520
toward the magnetic field direction.

573
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:03,840
Now, if you use a single loop, the

574
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:05,520
magnetic field strength is small. But if

575
00:22:03,840 --> 00:22:08,080
you wind many loops together, for

576
00:22:05,520 --> 00:22:10,640
example, a coil with a 100 turns, the

577
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:12,240
magnetic field becomes roughly 100 times

578
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:14,000
stronger.

579
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:16,320
That's the basic principle behind

580
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:18,320
electromagnets and in our case, gradient

581
00:22:16,320 --> 00:22:19,919
coils. On the left side of the figure,

582
00:22:18,320 --> 00:22:22,080
you see a loop with current flowing

583
00:22:19,919 --> 00:22:24,320
upward, generating a magnetic field that

584
00:22:22,080 --> 00:22:26,320
points to the right. On the right side,

585
00:22:24,320 --> 00:22:28,480
the current direction is reversed,

586
00:22:26,320 --> 00:22:30,400
producing a magnetic field that points

587
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:31,840
to the left.

588
00:22:30,400 --> 00:22:33,679
When we place these two coils

589
00:22:31,840 --> 00:22:35,600
symmetrically and run equal but opposite

590
00:22:33,679 --> 00:22:37,280
currents, something interesting happens.

591
00:22:35,600 --> 00:22:39,039
At the center between the coils, the

592
00:22:37,280 --> 00:22:42,080
magnetic fields cancel each other out,

593
00:22:39,039 --> 00:22:44,159
giving a field strength near zero.

594
00:22:42,080 --> 00:22:46,080
But if you move slightly to one side,

595
00:22:44,159 --> 00:22:48,000
one field becomes stronger while the

596
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:50,080
other becomes weaker. That means the

597
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:52,080
magnetic field increases linearly as you

598
00:22:50,080 --> 00:22:54,080
move away from the center. Exactly the

599
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:56,480
gradient we need.

600
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:58,640
So in the central region the total field

601
00:22:56,480 --> 00:23:00,480
varies in a nearly linear fashion even

602
00:22:58,640 --> 00:23:02,960
though the actual fields from each coil

603
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:04,960
are curved. This linear section is the

604
00:23:02,960 --> 00:23:06,640
useful part of the gradient field for

605
00:23:04,960 --> 00:23:08,799
imaging.

606
00:23:06,640 --> 00:23:11,120
In summary, a single loop of current

607
00:23:08,799 --> 00:23:12,880
generates a circular magnetic field.

608
00:23:11,120 --> 00:23:15,039
Multiple loops amplify the field

609
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:17,200
strength. Two symmetric oppositely

610
00:23:15,039 --> 00:23:19,600
oriented coils produce a linear gradient

611
00:23:17,200 --> 00:23:22,240
in the central region. That's the simple

612
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:24,799
physical idea behind how gradient coils

613
00:23:22,240 --> 00:23:26,480
work. elegant, practical, and directly

614
00:23:24,799 --> 00:23:31,400
derived from the basic laws of

615
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:31,400
electromagnetism you learned in school.

616
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:36,640
Now, let's connect this idea to the

617
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:38,640
actual gradient coils used in MRI

618
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:40,559
scanners. The linear field that we just

619
00:23:38,640 --> 00:23:42,640
discussed is formed between two opposing

620
00:23:40,559 --> 00:23:44,960
magnetic fields created by the left and

621
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:46,880
right coil pairs.

622
00:23:44,960 --> 00:23:49,840
That configuration generates the Z

623
00:23:46,880 --> 00:23:52,000
gradient field. However, for the X and Y

624
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:53,760
gradients, we can't arrange the coils in

625
00:23:52,000 --> 00:23:55,440
the same way because the patient needs

626
00:23:53,760 --> 00:23:57,120
to pass through the tunnel of the

627
00:23:55,440 --> 00:23:59,280
magnet.

628
00:23:57,120 --> 00:24:00,799
So, the coil design must be adjusted

629
00:23:59,280 --> 00:24:03,200
while keeping the same physical

630
00:24:00,799 --> 00:24:05,600
principle. For the Y gradient, the setup

631
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:07,919
uses a top coil and a bottom coil. Each

632
00:24:05,600 --> 00:24:09,760
coil forms what's called a saddle-shaped

633
00:24:07,919 --> 00:24:12,640
loop, but it still maintains a closed

634
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:14,720
current path. The magnetic field from

635
00:24:12,640 --> 00:24:16,480
the top coil points downward, while the

636
00:24:14,720 --> 00:24:18,559
field from the bottom coil points

637
00:24:16,480 --> 00:24:20,480
upward. In the middle, these two fields

638
00:24:18,559 --> 00:24:23,520
cancel each other, creating a region of

639
00:24:20,480 --> 00:24:25,440
zero field. As you move upward, the

640
00:24:23,520 --> 00:24:27,200
downward field weakens and the upward

641
00:24:25,440 --> 00:24:29,600
field strengthens, forming a linear

642
00:24:27,200 --> 00:24:31,760
yradient. If we rotate this entire

643
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:34,000
configuration by 90°, we can generate

644
00:24:31,760 --> 00:24:35,520
the X gradient using exactly the same

645
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:37,760
concept.

646
00:24:35,520 --> 00:24:39,840
When all these coil systems, the X, Y,

647
00:24:37,760 --> 00:24:41,919
and Z gradients are combined, we can

648
00:24:39,840 --> 00:24:45,600
generate any arbitrary gradient field,

649
00:24:41,919 --> 00:24:47,440
often represented as gx, gy, and gzed.

650
00:24:45,600 --> 00:24:49,200
By carefully controlling the current in

651
00:24:47,440 --> 00:24:50,720
each set of coils, we can produce

652
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:53,360
gradients in any direction or

653
00:24:50,720 --> 00:24:55,520
combination needed for imaging.

654
00:24:53,360 --> 00:24:57,279
In practice, the gradient coils are

655
00:24:55,520 --> 00:24:59,279
designed in multiple layers and

656
00:24:57,279 --> 00:25:01,279
additional shim coils are included to

657
00:24:59,279 --> 00:25:03,600
fine-tune the magnetic field so it

658
00:25:01,279 --> 00:25:05,840
remains as linear as possible within the

659
00:25:03,600 --> 00:25:07,760
imaging region. Although the engineering

660
00:25:05,840 --> 00:25:10,400
details are complex, the fundamental

661
00:25:07,760 --> 00:25:12,480
idea is simple. Using Maxwell's

662
00:25:10,400 --> 00:25:14,240
equations, just four equations that

663
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:16,320
describe how electric and magnetic

664
00:25:14,240 --> 00:25:18,720
fields behave, we can simulate the

665
00:25:16,320 --> 00:25:20,640
magnetic field using finite element

666
00:25:18,720 --> 00:25:22,720
computation.

667
00:25:20,640 --> 00:25:24,799
By adjusting coil shapes, adding new

668
00:25:22,720 --> 00:25:26,880
loops, and fine-tuning current paths,

669
00:25:24,799 --> 00:25:29,039
engineers can iteratively refine the

670
00:25:26,880 --> 00:25:31,120
field design until it achieves excellent

671
00:25:29,039 --> 00:25:32,880
linearity.

672
00:25:31,120 --> 00:25:34,960
So, even though the hardware looks

673
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:37,039
complicated, the underlying physics is

674
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:38,960
straightforward. We excite the coils in

675
00:25:37,039 --> 00:25:41,039
such a way that their combined fields

676
00:25:38,960 --> 00:25:43,679
produce the precise gradient patterns

677
00:25:41,039 --> 00:25:45,520
required for MRI imaging. And one final

678
00:25:43,679 --> 00:25:47,279
point, during imaging, these gradient

679
00:25:45,520 --> 00:25:48,960
coils rapidly switch on and off,

680
00:25:47,279 --> 00:25:50,880
producing mechanical stress that makes

681
00:25:48,960 --> 00:25:53,120
the loud knocking sounds we hear during

682
00:25:50,880 --> 00:25:54,720
MRI scans.

683
00:25:53,120 --> 00:25:56,880
That's the practical side of how

684
00:25:54,720 --> 00:25:59,880
gradient coils work both physically and

685
00:25:56,880 --> 00:25:59,880
acoustically.

686
00:26:01,600 --> 00:26:05,760
Now let's talk about the B1 field which

687
00:26:04,080 --> 00:26:07,760
is the missing component. we haven't

688
00:26:05,760 --> 00:26:11,440
discussed yet. This field is generated

689
00:26:07,760 --> 00:26:14,080
by the radio frequency coil or RF coil.

690
00:26:11,440 --> 00:26:16,320
The most common type of RF coil used for

691
00:26:14,080 --> 00:26:19,039
transmitting the B1 field is called a

692
00:26:16,320 --> 00:26:20,799
bird cage coil shown on the left. You

693
00:26:19,039 --> 00:26:22,640
can understand this coil design quite

694
00:26:20,799 --> 00:26:24,559
intuitively.

695
00:26:22,640 --> 00:26:27,120
It looks like the frame of a cylindrical

696
00:26:24,559 --> 00:26:29,200
cage. A circular structure with evenly

697
00:26:27,120 --> 00:26:31,520
spaced conducting bars connected at both

698
00:26:29,200 --> 00:26:33,360
ends by rings. When an alternating

699
00:26:31,520 --> 00:26:35,679
current flows through these bars, it

700
00:26:33,360 --> 00:26:39,279
creates a rotating magnetic field inside

701
00:26:35,679 --> 00:26:41,120
the ball. This rotating field is the B1

702
00:26:39,279 --> 00:26:44,000
field which is applied perpendicular to

703
00:26:41,120 --> 00:26:45,679
the main magnetic field B 0. The B1

704
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:47,600
field is responsible for exciting the

705
00:26:45,679 --> 00:26:50,159
protons and flipping the magnetization

706
00:26:47,600 --> 00:26:51,840
vector M away from its alignment with B

707
00:26:50,159 --> 00:26:53,440
0.

708
00:26:51,840 --> 00:26:55,919
On the right side of the slide, you can

709
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:57,760
see other kinds of RF coils as well. The

710
00:26:55,919 --> 00:26:59,679
surface coil shown in the middle is used

711
00:26:57,760 --> 00:27:01,600
for imaging regions close to the surface

712
00:26:59,679 --> 00:27:03,679
of the body, for example, the shoulder

713
00:27:01,600 --> 00:27:05,600
or knee. Because it's placed near the

714
00:27:03,679 --> 00:27:08,400
area of interest, it gives excellent

715
00:27:05,600 --> 00:27:11,679
signal to noise ratio locally, though it

716
00:27:08,400 --> 00:27:13,440
doesn't cover deep tissues as well. The

717
00:27:11,679 --> 00:27:15,840
third design shown on the right is a

718
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:18,000
phased array coil. This one combines

719
00:27:15,840 --> 00:27:20,400
multiple small coil elements arranged in

720
00:27:18,000 --> 00:27:22,080
an array. Each coil picks up signals

721
00:27:20,400 --> 00:27:23,840
from a different region and the signals

722
00:27:22,080 --> 00:27:26,000
are combined by the system to produce a

723
00:27:23,840 --> 00:27:28,320
highquality image.

724
00:27:26,000 --> 00:27:30,400
Phazed arrays are very useful for spine

725
00:27:28,320 --> 00:27:32,240
imaging and other applications where we

726
00:27:30,400 --> 00:27:34,799
need both wide coverage and high

727
00:27:32,240 --> 00:27:37,120
sensitivity. In summary, the bird cage

728
00:27:34,799 --> 00:27:39,919
coil is typically used for transmission.

729
00:27:37,120 --> 00:27:42,480
It creates a uniform B1 field, ideal for

730
00:27:39,919 --> 00:27:44,720
brain or whole body imaging.

731
00:27:42,480 --> 00:27:46,640
The surface coil is best for localized

732
00:27:44,720 --> 00:27:49,279
highresolution scans near the body

733
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:51,360
surface. The phased array coil allows us

734
00:27:49,279 --> 00:27:54,480
to combine multiple receiver channels

735
00:27:51,360 --> 00:27:57,039
for stronger and faster imaging.

736
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:59,600
So the RF coils are essential for both

737
00:27:57,039 --> 00:28:02,240
transmitting the B1 excitation field and

738
00:27:59,600 --> 00:28:03,840
receiving the MRI signal from the body,

739
00:28:02,240 --> 00:28:08,760
making them one of the most important

740
00:28:03,840 --> 00:28:08,760
components in the entire imaging chain.

741
00:28:10,080 --> 00:28:14,880
Now let's take a closer look at how the

742
00:28:11,679 --> 00:28:16,720
Burage coil produces a uniform B1 field.

743
00:28:14,880 --> 00:28:20,000
If you consider the two cross-sections

744
00:28:16,720 --> 00:28:22,000
shown here, the idea is quite intuitive.

745
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:23,919
When the current in one connecting wire

746
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:25,760
flows in a particular direction, it

747
00:28:23,919 --> 00:28:27,840
generates a local magnetic field

748
00:28:25,760 --> 00:28:29,679
pointing downward.

749
00:28:27,840 --> 00:28:31,840
To produce a local field pointing

750
00:28:29,679 --> 00:28:33,600
upward, the current in the adjacent wire

751
00:28:31,840 --> 00:28:35,840
must flow in the opposite direction,

752
00:28:33,600 --> 00:28:37,760
forming a closed loop. This basic

753
00:28:35,840 --> 00:28:39,520
configuration, currents flowing in

754
00:28:37,760 --> 00:28:41,360
opposite directions through adjacent

755
00:28:39,520 --> 00:28:43,120
loops, creates magnetic fields that

756
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:45,200
point downward in some regions and

757
00:28:43,120 --> 00:28:47,200
upward in others.

758
00:28:45,200 --> 00:28:49,039
When multiple loops or cross-sections

759
00:28:47,200 --> 00:28:51,120
are added around the cylinder, these

760
00:28:49,039 --> 00:28:53,520
individual magnetic fields combine to

761
00:28:51,120 --> 00:28:56,240
form a uniform field across the entire

762
00:28:53,520 --> 00:28:58,240
region inside the coil.

763
00:28:56,240 --> 00:29:00,559
Mathematically, this can be shown by

764
00:28:58,240 --> 00:29:02,559
modulating the current as a sinosoidal

765
00:29:00,559 --> 00:29:04,880
function of the angular position which

766
00:29:02,559 --> 00:29:07,840
we call phi. If you plot the current

767
00:29:04,880 --> 00:29:10,240
intensity as a function of the fi angle,

768
00:29:07,840 --> 00:29:13,200
it varies like a sine wave starting from

769
00:29:10,240 --> 00:29:15,520
zero at phi equals 0 degrees, reaching a

770
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:18,799
maximum at 90° and then becoming

771
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:21,279
negative at 180°.

772
00:29:18,799 --> 00:29:23,360
This sinosoidal modulation ensures that

773
00:29:21,279 --> 00:29:25,679
the magnetic field intensity remains

774
00:29:23,360 --> 00:29:27,919
uniform across the cross-section. To

775
00:29:25,679 --> 00:29:30,000
make the B1 field rotate in space, the

776
00:29:27,919 --> 00:29:32,000
current itself is also modulated over

777
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:33,919
time so that the maximum and minimum of

778
00:29:32,000 --> 00:29:37,200
the field continuously move around the

779
00:29:33,919 --> 00:29:38,960
coil. As a result, the B1 field rotates

780
00:29:37,200 --> 00:29:41,440
smoothly, allowing it to flip the

781
00:29:38,960 --> 00:29:44,240
magnetization vector M in a controlled

782
00:29:41,440 --> 00:29:45,919
and consistent way during excitation. In

783
00:29:44,240 --> 00:29:48,000
essence, this is how we achieve a

784
00:29:45,919 --> 00:29:50,399
uniform rotating magnetic field that

785
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:53,760
interacts with the main B 0 field.

786
00:29:50,399 --> 00:29:56,720
Together the B 0 field, B1 field and the

787
00:29:53,760 --> 00:29:58,880
three gradient fields G subX, G suby,

788
00:29:56,720 --> 00:30:01,120
and G subzed form the complete

789
00:29:58,880 --> 00:30:02,640
electromagnetic environment of the MRI

790
00:30:01,120 --> 00:30:05,200
system.

791
00:30:02,640 --> 00:30:07,760
What's truly fascinating is that all of

792
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:09,600
these ideas, the generation of magnetic

793
00:30:07,760 --> 00:30:11,840
fields, their directions, and the way

794
00:30:09,600 --> 00:30:14,399
they add up can actually be explained

795
00:30:11,840 --> 00:30:16,320
using high school physics, Ampair's law,

796
00:30:14,399 --> 00:30:18,559
the right- hand rule, and the principle

797
00:30:16,320 --> 00:30:20,880
of superposition.

798
00:30:18,559 --> 00:30:22,720
Of course, for real MRI coil design, we

799
00:30:20,880 --> 00:30:24,880
need precise optimization to make sure

800
00:30:22,720 --> 00:30:26,559
the fields are uniform and stable.

801
00:30:24,880 --> 00:30:28,720
That's done through finite element

802
00:30:26,559 --> 00:30:30,720
analysis, a numerical technique that

803
00:30:28,720 --> 00:30:32,559
lets engineers compute the detailed

804
00:30:30,720 --> 00:30:35,760
magnetic field distribution and

805
00:30:32,559 --> 00:30:37,600
fine-tune the geometry of the coil.

806
00:30:35,760 --> 00:30:39,440
So, while the physical concept is

807
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:41,600
beautifully simple, the practical

808
00:30:39,440 --> 00:30:45,640
realization requires sophisticated

809
00:30:41,600 --> 00:30:45,640
computation and engineering.

810
00:30:47,279 --> 00:30:51,200
Now let's look at what happens when we

811
00:30:49,039 --> 00:30:53,600
use a surface coil instead of a full

812
00:30:51,200 --> 00:30:56,000
bird cage coil that covers the entire

813
00:30:53,600 --> 00:30:58,240
patient. A surface coil is a smaller

814
00:30:56,000 --> 00:31:00,080
coil placed directly near the region of

815
00:30:58,240 --> 00:31:02,399
interest. For example, near the spinal

816
00:31:00,080 --> 00:31:04,080
cord or breast.

817
00:31:02,399 --> 00:31:06,559
Because it's positioned so close to the

818
00:31:04,080 --> 00:31:09,120
tissue, it produces a very strong B1

819
00:31:06,559 --> 00:31:11,039
field right next to the coil surface.

820
00:31:09,120 --> 00:31:12,720
However, the field strength drops off

821
00:31:11,039 --> 00:31:15,120
rapidly with distance as you can see

822
00:31:12,720 --> 00:31:17,360
from the plot on the left.

823
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:19,360
So the signal intensity is highest near

824
00:31:17,360 --> 00:31:21,520
the coil and becomes much weaker for

825
00:31:19,360 --> 00:31:23,279
tissues deeper inside the body. This

826
00:31:21,520 --> 00:31:25,440
makes surface coils particularly useful

827
00:31:23,279 --> 00:31:27,360
for localized imaging where we only need

828
00:31:25,440 --> 00:31:30,320
highquality signals from a specific

829
00:31:27,360 --> 00:31:31,840
region such as the spine or breast.

830
00:31:30,320 --> 00:31:34,159
They are also very important for

831
00:31:31,840 --> 00:31:35,679
parallel MRI where multiple small coils

832
00:31:34,159 --> 00:31:37,519
are used together to collect data

833
00:31:35,679 --> 00:31:39,840
simultaneously from different parts of

834
00:31:37,519 --> 00:31:42,080
the body. This parallel setup helps

835
