2607
01:39:44,480 --> 01:39:49,840
inside the body by detecting radiation

2608
01:39:46,800 --> 01:39:52,400
emitted from injected traces.

2609
01:39:49,840 --> 01:39:54,639
Now in this work we take the concept one

2610
01:39:52,400 --> 01:39:56,719
step further by combining emission and

2611
01:39:54,639 --> 01:39:59,040
transmission tomography into a single

2612
01:39:56,719 --> 01:40:01,040
simultaneous process what we call

2613
01:39:59,040 --> 01:40:03,679
simultaneous emission transmission

2614
01:40:01,040 --> 01:40:06,080
tomography or CT.

2615
01:40:03,679 --> 01:40:08,000
This idea was presented at the fully 3D

2616
01:40:06,080 --> 01:40:10,000
conference in can China and it

2617
01:40:08,000 --> 01:40:12,239
represents an important advance in

2618
01:40:10,000 --> 01:40:14,719
multimodal imaging.

2619
01:40:12,239 --> 01:40:16,800
Normally in PET or spec emission data

2620
01:40:14,719 --> 01:40:18,960
and transmission data are collected

2621
01:40:16,800 --> 01:40:21,119
separately. First one scan for anatomy

2622
01:40:18,960 --> 01:40:23,119
and then another for function. But with

2623
01:40:21,119 --> 01:40:26,239
set both types of data are acquired at

2624
01:40:23,119 --> 01:40:28,400
the same time. By combining emission and

2625
01:40:26,239 --> 01:40:29,760
transmission information simultaneously,

2626
01:40:28,400 --> 01:40:31,679
we can achieve more accurate

2627
01:40:29,760 --> 01:40:34,159
reconstructions with improved spatial

2628
01:40:31,679 --> 01:40:36,159
and contrast resolution. The images on

2629
01:40:34,159 --> 01:40:38,080
the left show the structural information

2630
01:40:36,159 --> 01:40:39,760
from the transmission data, while the

2631
01:40:38,080 --> 01:40:42,719
ones on the right display emission

2632
01:40:39,760 --> 01:40:44,800
activity from the radio tracer.

2633
01:40:42,719 --> 01:40:46,960
When we fuse these two data sets, we

2634
01:40:44,800 --> 01:40:49,199
obtain both anatomical and functional

2635
01:40:46,960 --> 01:40:50,880
information in a single scan, reducing

2636
01:40:49,199 --> 01:40:53,280
motion artifacts and improving

2637
01:40:50,880 --> 01:40:55,360
quantitative accuracy.

2638
01:40:53,280 --> 01:40:57,840
This represents another step toward our

2639
01:40:55,360 --> 01:40:59,679
